@startuml
title UML State Machine Diagram

state StartChoice <<choice>>
state AdminChoice <<choice>>
state EditorChoice <<choice>>
state ReadFeedbackChoice <<choice>>
state EndJoin <<choice>>

[*] --> StartChoice
StartChoice --> Register
StartChoice --> Login

Register --> AdminChoice
Login --> EditorChoice

AdminChoice --> ManageProfiles
AdminChoice --> InvalidUser
ManageProfiles --> Publishing
InvalidUser --> [*]

EditorChoice --> Writing
EditorChoice --> Editing
EditorChoice --> InvalidUser
Writing --> Editing
Editing --> Publishing

Publishing --> Reading
Reading --> Reading

Search --> Search
Reading --> ReadFeedbackChoice
ReadFeedbackChoice --> Feedback
Feedback --> EndJoin

EndJoin --> [*]

state Admin <<extends ManageProfiles>>
Admin : do / Manage profile in database
Admin : do / Add, delete or edit profiles if necessary

state Editor <<extends Writing & Editing>>
Editor : do / Write article
Editor : do / Edit article

state User <<extends Login>>
User : entry / Registered user
User : do / Enter login credentials
User : exit / Valid username and password

state Writer <<extends User>>
Writer : entry / Writer logged in
Writer : do / Write article
Writer : exit / Send to editor

state Moderator <<extends Editor>>
Moderator : entry / Editor logged in and article to be edited
Moderator : do / Edit article
Moderator : exit / Send to moderator/admin

state Publisher <<extends Admin & Moderator>>
Publisher : entry / Admin logged in and article to be approved
Publisher : do / Choose to approve and publish or reject article
Publisher : do / Add article to database if approved
Publisher : exit / Publish article

state Reader <<extends User>>
Reader : entry / Published article
Reader : do / Read article
Reader : exit / Completed reading

state FeedbackGiver <<extends Reader>>
FeedbackGiver : entry / Reader chosen to give feedback
FeedbackGiver : do / Get feedback
FeedbackGiver : exit / Feedback entry successful
@enduml
